Package: bitcalc
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Nyang'ada Stone Bradley <ridddle5050@gmail.com>
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: bash (>= 4.4)
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/ridddle-en/bitcalc
Description: bitwise calculator and base converter with step-by-step output
 Hardware-engineering toolkit: binary arithmetic with carry/borrow/overflow
 flags, logic  operations with truth tables, shifts and rotates (negative
 counts reverse direction), two's complement, byte swap, population count, 
 BCD/Gray code and fractional base conversion. Shows the working as aligned
 bit rows, or prints only the answer for use in pipelines.
